{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026","id":1208790,"title":"Lore In Your Games, or, Gurus Gone Wyld\u2026","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-19T03:39:57-07:00","id":1208790,"title":"Lore In Your Games, or, Gurus Gone Wyld\u2026","content":"Having built my new sorcerer PC, Spider, as Lore Supernal, I'd like to hear from other players and STs about their experience with the rules for Introducing Facts. <br /> <br /> -Players, what sorts of declarations have you gotten away with making? <br /> <br /> -STs, what's the wildest introduced fact you've allowed? <br /> <br /> -What sort of difficulties have you assigned/had to overcome? <br /> <br /> -What's the most trouble a declared fact has ever gotten you into?<br /> <br /> -Do I deserve to be gruesomely murdered for that awful pun? (Yes, yes I do.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-19-2018, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T05:12:40-07:00","id":1208807,"title":"","content":"As long as it flows with the story... then you can tell them anything. It also helps if you just, as ST, seem confident in your presention. You are, after all, telling a story.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> I mix in a little swahili and other exotic verbage when describing southern locations and whatnot.<br /> <br /> So when I give my players what at first looks like a fetch-quest to get some royal prince hiding in a village, to return him to the king's royal war camp for his special forces it might go like<br /> <br /> &quot;The king's vizier informs you [the circle]: You are to retrieve Prince Usiku from the village from Maleli - do so quietly! He has been living there in secret - he thinks he's an orphan and doesn't know of his birthright, but our enemies will no doubt also be looking for him. He needs to be bought to the ikanda to the west of the city so he can learn and live agoge until he is of age to join the court. Now go&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes I took &quot;ikanda&quot; and &quot;agoge&quot; from Civ 6 - it's a great game to steal cool terms from.<br /> <br /> point is - that the above, delivered with certainty and confidence will very much so make any player think &quot;Hell yes, this is what we're doing!&quot; - never mind that I just dropped hints of how the local king seems to be hiding his children among the civil populace to keep them safe in their youth, or hinted of the king's war camp or the warrior culture he fosters among his soldiers.<br /> <br /> It's the closest you can really do to show, not tell - when you're playing a P&amp;P RPG.<br /> <br /> It's the exact opposite of an exposition dump - it's a quest description with lore sprinkled through it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> When you fuck up on that you get into trouble - either because it might strain your player's suspension of disbelief, or because a massive and boring info-dump might easily be forgotten.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for wildest fact introduced? Probably some of the fluff I threw at a former group of players when they arrived in Yu-Shan for the first time - they were awestruck.<br /> <br /> AS for most trouble from a declared fact? I told a player that yes, conservation of momentum exists in the game unless I say otherwise, combined with me having previously given a rough weight estimate of a yeddim. Said player then calculated the force of impact that a steel-armored Yeddim going full solar flying yeddim rocket. This was then swiftly used to absolutely DESTROY two flying DBs in dragon armor. Sure, it also pulped the yeddim, but those can be replaced. Engineering students make for &quot;fun&quot; players.<br /> <br /> and then my players had two suits of dragon armor. Oh boy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":588,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","user":"webkilla","date":". 04-19-2018, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T05:22:29-07:00","id":1208811,"title":"","content":"Um, you seem to have misunderstood me - I'm talking about the system for <i>players</i> introducing facts, via the Lore rules in the new edition.<br /> <br /> I mostly end up behind the ST screen when doing games of Exalted, so I wanted to gauge others' use of it.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I <i>really like</i> the system. &quot;Knowledge is power,&quot; as they say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-19-2018, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T05:29:16-07:00","id":1208812,"title":"","content":"My players have never even attempted it. They seem to be stuck in traditional rpg setup where lore is dumped on the players by the ST. Even when I specifically point it out as an option they tend say &quot;Huh, that's cool,&quot; and promptly forget about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T06:14:17-07:00","id":1208829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026#post1208790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Players, what sorts of declarations have you gotten away with making?</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;in the southwestern border of the wasting tundra&gt; &quot;Shit, that mistake means a wyld hunt is likely to be called on us by the next month. How the hell do we get to Ascension and at the same time mislead the hunters?&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, this mountain range is very close to an Ice Roc soar, if we make it look like we got killed by their swoops and tame a couple of them we should travel much faster and with no ground trail&quot;<br /> &lt;the other fact-introducer, to the dawn icewalker monster hunter&gt; &quot;One of your sister icewalker tribes tames ice rocs by stealing their prey and winning the fight over it with flashy displays of domination, doesn't it?&quot;<br /> &lt;dawn&gt; &quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026#post1208790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-STs, what's the wildest introduced fact you've allowed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, my players are relatively tame in their introductions...<ul><li>they've created bureaucratic loopholes to support Threaten actions</li> <li>made cultural trivia that facilitates creating a certain context in parties</li> <li>established a rivalry between most local grain storage services to support their plan to buy all of them...</li> </ul><br /> <br /> It should get wilder after the current story when they return to their &quot;home city&quot; because the Chronicler decided she'll become the personal biographer of the satrap, who suspects she's anathema, but hasn't acted on it because they're both very cautious and the last inquisition she started to catch the pc caught a fair folk that was doing almost everything that made her suspect the Chronicler.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026#post1208790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-What sort of difficulties have you assigned/had to overcome?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it feels easy it's 1 or 2. Most range around 3-5, but I don't cap the difficulty anywhere, just need to see how far-fectched they can get.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026#post1208790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-What's the most trouble a declared fact has ever gotten you into?</div> </div> </div> </div>One time we were hunting a raksha that kidnapped people, maddened their families, and returned using those people as a very specific type of slave labor without eating their souls.<br /> In combat with it (was a very tough fight, we didn't want to prolong it further) we declared that kind of &quot;haunt&quot; fair folk was particularly amenable and loyal to certain terms of surrender.<br /> It surrendered, us in return promising his story would live on beyond his freehold's range. Because of...complications... we killed it anyway, but our alchemist intended to keep good on the promise, for he gave us directions to the freehold.<br /> The twilight anima-exploded himself into that very freehold because of that fight, and when we came to her rescue we caught ourselves with conflicting promises: that raksha's master was pissed off we killed his Storyteller and in his death wanted to keep his tales to himself only, and demanded we kept secret about him in return for releasing our Professor without a fight. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026#post1208790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Do I deserve to be gruesomely murdered for that awful pun? (Yes, yes I do.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-19-2018, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T06:45:30-07:00","id":1208836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026?p=1208812#post1208812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My players have never even attempted it. They seem to be stuck in traditional rpg setup where lore is dumped on the players by the ST. Even when I specifically point it out as an option they tend say &quot;Huh, that's cool,&quot; and promptly forget about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here.<br /> <br /> Only one player ever tried doing it, he declared a god existed. The god of something or other in the south (something not canonically decided), I forget what.<br /> <br /> That seems like the sort of thing that works pretty well, as it lets PCs fill in the world a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-19-2018, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T07:50:43-07:00","id":1208866,"title":"","content":"I really look forward to seeing this thread grow - and I hope this isn't off-topic - but those of you with &quot;crazy lore gurus&quot;, do you have any tricks or techniques or experiences that helped nurture that? Did <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar32_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"32\" data-vbnamecard=\"32\">Synapse</a> have any stepping stone experiences that led the group to really embrace Lore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T07:54:08-07:00","id":1208869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026?p=1208866#post1208866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really look forward to seeing this thread grow - and I hope this isn't off-topic - but those of you with &quot;crazy lore gurus&quot;, do you have any tricks or techniques or experiences that helped nurture that? Did <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar32_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"32\" data-vbnamecard=\"32\">Synapse</a> have any stepping stone experiences that led the group to really embrace Lore?</div> </div> </div> </div>For a while any time I felt the players were stuck pondering how to tackle a problem I'd say &quot;this is the kind of situation good fact-introduction tears apart&quot;. Sometimes they'd still be stuck, sometimes they'd come up with nice ideas. They got better at it.<br /> <br /> Then there was this time the Chronicler introduced the fact that goats have an animosity towards cows, considering themselves superior, and herders that want to raise both have to take care on how they place and care for their animals or either might get stressed. For the sole purpose of continuing a joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T07:59:32-07:00","id":1208873,"title":"","content":"Let\u2019s see,in the game I am playing in we\u2019ve established:<br /> <br /> 1) The Secret Origin of Zoatham<br /> 2) The location of multiple Manses including one responsible for directing weather patterns in the South<br /> 3) That Urim was actually built by Sidereals<br /> 4) That Elementals don\u2019t gain Sapience until Essence 3<br /> 5) on a BOTCH That what a player was trying to establish as a swear word for sidereals was actually a term of endearment<br /> <br /> And many more. When I get home I\u2019ll post some more examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T08:32:47-07:00","id":1208888,"title":"","content":"When my party and I brought 30-odd people liberated from the Lintha to a shore town in 3 Tidemares, I introduced a fact that it's good luck in the West to see Tidemares at sunset, so no one gave the approaching elementals any mind. That was fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 04-19-2018, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T09:33:48-07:00","id":1208916,"title":"","content":"Dammit, I thought I destroyed all those records...Look, it was the Calibration Festival, it was the Cerulean Lute, we'd all just got off after a month of overtime fieldwork and needed to blow off some steam, and anyways inviting the Suzerain of Dancing Portraits wasn't my idea, but even if it had been it's not like the Loom can't handle a few...oh. Oh, this is about introducing facts with Lore.<br /> <br /> ...carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T01:23:27-07:00","id":1209142,"title":"","content":"I tend to tell my players that they should be introducing facts more, but now that I'm playing in a game I haven't done it yet either...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T01:57:12-07:00","id":1209152,"title":"","content":"My players have introduced several things, mostly small factoids that gave them temporary advantages. Nothing too game-breaking.<br /> <br /> For example, the group was being pursued by political opponents out for blood. One character used their knowledge of local geography to bring up a possible hillock they could fight from the top of, in order to gain terrain advantages.<br /> <br /> After the fight, one of their companions was direly wounded, and they had to bring them back to town before a winter storm set in. They ended up not making it, and the geographically-knowledgeable character introduced a hot spring where they could take shelter.<br /> <br /> So on and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T03:05:02-07:00","id":1209160,"title":"","content":"I've never actually been a player. Because of that I'm personally inclined to build a combat monster just so that I can revel in the power. If I also make that crazy character good at Lore I would introduce facts to make fights more dangerous and interesting. Maybe some facts about the terrain, or even give monsters new and dangerous attacks.<br /> <br /> Everyone knows that Cthulhu is the high priest of his religion, what most people don't know is that when he goes into battle he wears a gigantic suit of power armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","user":"Hark","date":". 04-20-2018, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T04:49:41-07:00","id":1209178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026?p=1209160#post1209160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never actually been a player. Because of that I'm personally inclined to build a combat monster just so that I can revel in the power. If I also make that crazy character good at Lore I would introduce facts to make fights more dangerous and interesting. Maybe some facts about the terrain, or even give monsters new and dangerous attacks.<br /> <br /> Everyone knows that Cthulhu is the high priest of his religion, what most people don't know is that when he goes into battle he wears a gigantic suit of power armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps give you ideas, my berserker-necromancer is going to delve into lore just enough to get first knowledge's grace, truth-rendering gaze and maybe heaven-turning calculations to support war:<br /> 1) FKG allows my tiger warrior training technique to train my zombie hordes into elite soldiers<br /> 2) TRG is great for stratagems and navigation<br /> 3) HTC is auxiliary to necromancy<br /> <br /> You want a lich king? This is how you get a lich king.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-20-2018, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:06:18-07:00","id":1209228,"title":"","content":"Hah, I never thought of using FKG with Tiger Warrior Training, but that does make perfect sense. And work really well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:46:22-07:00","id":1209243,"title":"","content":"Our group basically made up all the facts about Vaneha. It got sort of silly at some points. I personally do try and introduce facts pretty consistently but with lore 1 and int 2 I am not being very successful this time around!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:58:49-07:00","id":1209248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026?p=1209228#post1209228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hah, I never thought of using FKG with Tiger Warrior Training, but that does make perfect sense. And work really well.</div> </div> </div> </div>2nd circle necromancy used to, and certainly will in 3e, summon intelligent undead and mindless hordes. So you get badass undead troops and your own loyal death knights.<br /> Seriously, the only reason I don't stat up a Frostmourne for Ivory Wasp is because she has Stormcaller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:00:18-07:00","id":1209249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208790-lore-in-your-games-or-gurus-gone-wyld\u2026?p=1209178#post1209178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it helps give you ideas, my berserker-necromancer is going to delve into lore just enough to get first knowledge's grace, truth-rendering gaze and maybe heaven-turning calculations to support war:<br /> 1) FKG allows my tiger warrior training technique to train my zombie hordes into elite soldiers<br /> 2) TRG is great for stratagems and navigation<br /> 3) HTC is auxiliary to necromancy<br /> <br /> You want a lich king? This is how you get a lich king.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite what I had in mind, but interesting idea.<br /> <br /> I was thinking more along the lines of, &quot;Jimmy, did you know that the lions inhabiting this region can change colour much like a chameleon, and have venomous claws? Scholars believe it may have been the result of a Wyld incursion centuries ago.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, &quot;Hey Jimmy, did you know the local skunk population is special? One of the Anathema from before the Great Usurpation cross-bred them with foxes to give them a more pleasant appearance and then altered their scent glands to produce a pleasant aromatic musk. There was however a dangerous side-effect. Those sprayed by the skunk are driven irreparably mad by hallucinations of talking skunks.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:18:52-07:00","id":1209257,"title":"","content":"Along the way you get the core fact-introduction charms, and since you were talking about enjoying a power trip or three...<br /> Later in Lore you get the Calamities too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T10:51:33-07:00","id":1218611,"title":"","content":"Well, yesterday I Introduced a Fact for the Great Forks game.<br /> <br /> &quot;The rich Dynast Cynis Hamon spent an inordinate amount of jade to put together a fantastical bestiary, a veritable zoo of impressive and dangerous creatures. Ox-dragons, pestletails, a pack of claw striders\u2026 it's even rumored that a pair of Wood Aspects brought him a tyrant lizard a few weeks back.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T13:39:01-07:00","id":1218673,"title":"","content":"Just had a player establish that animals can sniff out hearthstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T03:39:11-07:00","id":1218854,"title":"","content":"Our Sidereals recently established the universal greeting from Transformers the Movie &quot;bah weep granah weep nini bong&quot; as a nonsense phrase that's easy to reply to so strange creatures can identify themselves as self aware. After that the situation kind of got more ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T04:03:06-07:00","id":1218859,"title":"","content":"Oh, a fact I once introduced was that a group of corrupt Sijanese officials in Nexus were selling off the bones of poor dead people to the Nighthammer smelteries - as a source of carbon for the foundries...<br /> <br /> (never mind that bones aren't carbon, but my players thought it was cool and, well... rule of cool) - also it helped explain why certain blacksmith shops were getting haunted","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T07:12:30-07:00","id":1218898,"title":"","content":"Recently, we've been in my Zenith's homeland, the Plateau of Leng. Obviously, it's full of hideous monsters, goatmen, degenerate cultists, pre-human ruins, evil sorcerers, etc. We went to the Black Monastery of Leng to fight a Nephwrack, but it turns out he'd done an evil ritual and travelled through the Labyrinth to the Night Caste's Egypt-expy homeland, Sukhmet.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we returned to the Haslanti Twilight's airship to find it had been eaten by a giant worm-monster, leaving just the indigestible artefact-engine. So we were kind of stuck, as it would take 6 months' walk to get to Sukhmet.<br /> <br /> So, the other PCs all asked me if I knew where to find a sorcerer. Obviously, my Lore rating covered my own homeland. I felt that declaring that there was a lovely helpful sorcerer would be unthematic though, so I declared that there was an evil sorcerer who lived about 6 hours' walk away in his evil tower.<br /> <br /> I got like 6 or 7 successes, so the ST told me that N'amirah, Whose Black Yoke Enslaved the cities of Sybek, Peer of the Lord of Evil, had a giant basalt castle 6 hours walk away. We went and paid him a visit, tricked him into lending us his Demon-horse-pulled chariot, and sped off to Sukhmet. <br /> <br /> Though, as he was a debauched and incredibly jaded sorcerer whose main interest was turning beautiful people into statues and is desperate for something fun to do, I wouldn't be surprised if he later decides he wants to get revenge on us for tricking him.<br /> <br /> That was the first fact anyone introduced in the game, I think it went pretty well. The ST seemed happy with it, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}